\lang1033\b\f0 Project Files:\b0  \par
Command.cs\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720 It contains three classes InitializeCommand, UpdateParamsCommand and UpdateGeometryCommand. All of them implement interface IExternalCommand. \par
\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f0 ExternalApplication.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains one class ExternalApplication which implements interface IExternalApplication\f1 .\f0  This class will create one custom Ribbon panel contains three buttons to invoke the three external commands defined in Command.cs file. This class subscribes some application level events to update door parameters too. That can insure the doc is correct when it is about saved, saved as etc\f1 .\par
\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f0 DoorSwingData.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains one class DoorSwingData which prepares the needed data and updates door opening, Internal/External door and To/From Room information.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f1\par
\f0 DoorFamily.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains one class DoorFamily which maintains family name, family geometry and door opening expression information for each door family. And it also customizes the door opening expression according to each door family\rquote s geometry and country's standard.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f1\par
\f0 DoorFamilyGeometry.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains one class DoorGeometry which is used to transform Revit geometry data to appropriate format for GDI.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f1\par
\f0 DoorSharedParameters.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains one Static class DoorSharedParameters which is used to add three shared parameters to door and named with BasalOpening, InstanceOpening and Internal Door\f1 .\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\par
\f0 InitializeForm.cs\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\tx720\f0 This file contains a form class InitializeForm which consists of one DataGridView to show user all door families existent in current Revit project, and one pictureBox to show door family\rquote s geometry. User can customize door opening expression according to each door family\rquote s geometry and country's standard here\f1 .\par
\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\f0 DoorSwingResource.resx\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\f0 A resource file which contains some strings to identify the door opening.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\par
\b Description:\b0  \par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360 For door\rquote s opening functionality, user can invoke the external command "Customize Door Opening Expression" to add needed shared parameters and customize door opening expression according to their own country's standard and each door family\rquote s geometry. When the door was flipped or mirrored, user can invoke the external command \ldblquote Update Door Properties\rdblquote  to update parameters\rquote  values. Schedule for these parameters will be done from Revit UI.\par
\par
For door\rquote s related room functionality, from Revit UI user can schedule the \ldblquote To room\rdblquote  and \ldblquote From room\rdblquote  information for Internal and external doors in two separate schedule tables and can change the direction of the door in schedule tables. User will then use \ldblquote Update Door Geometry\rdblquote  command to update the geometry of the door after the direction of the door was changed in schedule tables. When the door was flipped or mirrored in view, user can invoke the external command \ldblquote Update Door Properties\rdblquote  to update \ldblquote To room\rdblquote  and \ldblquote From room\rdblquote  information too.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360 Parameter updating process will also be invoked upon closing, save or save as of the project file.\par
\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\b\f0 Instructions: \f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li360\tx360\b0\f0 1.\tab Prepare your Revit project\f1 .\f0  \par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360 Open or new a Revit project and make sure all needed rooms are placed. If your project file has any closed wall loop without a room being defined, the sample will have a dialog to ask you to confirm that you would consider doors bounding those areas as external doors.\f1\par
\f0 A sample project file DoorSwing.rvt is available in the sample\rquote s folder.\par
\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li360\tx360\f0 2.\tab Customize your door opening expression\f1 .\f0  \par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360 Click "Customize Door Opening Expression" command (menu item or Ribbon button) to customize each door family\rquote s opening expression based on the family\rquote s geometry and your country\rquote s standard. This is the first command of the sample. If the expressions which comply with your country standard are not available on the list, you can open the source code project and modify in the following 3 areas:\f1\par
\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\f0 a.\tab Edit project resource file.\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\f0 b.\tab Edit DoorSwingData static constructor in DoorSwingData.cs. Add more door opening expressions from resource file into OpeningTypes list.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720 c.\tab Edit UpdateOpeningFeatureOfOneDoor function in DoorSwingData.cs. Add more else if in \ldblquote if (switchesOpeningValueFlag)\{\'85\}\rdblquote  statement to deal with the added door opening expression\f1 .\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\par
\f0 Users who want to create a localized version of the sample can follow step 2.a above.\par
\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li360\tx360\f0 3.\tab Schedule the parameters\f1 .\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li360\f0 Create door schedule from Revit UI. You can schedule \ldblquote Opening\rdblquote  , \ldblquote Internal Door\rdblquote  parameters and \ldblquote Room number\rdblquote  of \ldblquote From Room\rdblquote /\rdblquote To Room\rdblquote  or any others you need\f1 .\par
\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-360\li720\tx720\f0 a.\tab Create Internal Door Schedule\f1 .\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li720\f0 Revit Button: View Tab->Create Panel->Schedules Button->Schedule/Quantities;\par
Category: Doors; Name: Internal Door Schedule\f1 .\par
\f0\par
Add parameters which need to be scheduled.\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-180\li900\tx900\f2\'b7\tab\f0 Add existing parameters: Mark, Internal Door, InstanceOpening, FromRoom:Number, ToRoom:Number;\f1\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\fi-180\li900\f2\'b7\tab\f0 Add a Calculated value: Name: Opening, Select: Formula, Discipline: Common, Type: Text, Formula: InstanceOpening\f1 .\par
\f2\'b7\tab\f0 Move up Opening parameter before InstanceOpening parameter\f1 .\par
\pard\ltrpar\nowidctlpar\li720\par
